  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Motors obligated $633M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. General Motors received 13,904 awards with an average award size of $45.5K, and obligations are up 124.6% year over year. These totals are contract obligations; the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables report total contract values rather than obligation flows. Obligations by fiscal year show a sequence of values: FY21 $187M, FY22 $188M, FY23 $260M, FY24 $182M, FY25 $282M, FY26 $633M. The FY2026 to date total is a partial fiscal-year figure and should be read as year-to-date obligations rather than a full-year total. General Motors' award count and average award size indicate a large number of relatively small awards alongside some larger, multi-year contracts captured in the separate largest-awards listings. Contractors and procurement teams should treat the FY26 jump in obligations as a current-year snapshot and cross-check contract-level tables when they need award-value or contract-expiration detail.",
